  "result": "I've found the archived tickets for this request and I'm writing up the answer now.\n\n{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#46232\", \"PowerToys#48211\", \"PowerToys#46668\"], \"answer\": \"This has been requested before. PowerToys#46232 ('Allow all system tray icons to be displayed on the dock') is the open tracking thread. Please add a thumbs-up there instead of opening a new issue. The maintainer said the PowerToys team probably can't ship tray-icon support in the Dock itself. They would welcome a third-party Command Palette extension that shows tray icons as a Dock band, and the thread points to YASB's systray implementation as a reference. PowerToys#48211 and #46668 were pointed to that same thread. Nothing in the archive says tray support is built yet, and the Dock is not planned as a full taskbar replacement. For now, keep using the Windows taskbar tray, or look for or build a community extension.\"}",
